TI ipc echo test
Pre-requisite: Need to load ipc echo test firmware image to remote cores.

Options:
     -v Get more verbose logs on the message sent and received.
     -s skip a pre-defined list of remote cores. This is needed for the standard
        configuration that we support on QNX where the MCU1_0 run DM firmware.
     -n Number of messages to be exchanged between A53 and each remote core.
     -p Do a negative test case, with no remotecores. This should report 0 pings once
        the test is complete.
     -m Multithread the send and receive threads with the send thread initiating
        pings every 1 ms.

Note:
    In case the remote cores are not loaded, the test is blocked since it is waiting
    for all the cores to complete exchanging messages before exiting.
